From: arch-xiaomi-sheng maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: read MAC address from firmware properties

Some platforms keep the factory address outside the WLAN board file and pass
it through firmware properties.  ath11k already supports this using
device_get_mac_address(), but ath12k falls back directly from an invalid WMI
address to a random address.

Read the standard IEEE 802.11 firmware property and prefer it when per-pdev WMI
addresses are unavailable.  Reference the common wireless DT schema so the
existing local-mac-address property is accepted by the ath12k binding.

Signed-off-by: arch-xiaomi-sheng maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 .../bindings/net/wireless/qcom,ath12k.yaml       | 3 +++
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c            | 7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/qcom,ath12k.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/qcom,ath12k.yaml
index dc68dd59a0cd..b696eebb15e3 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/qcom,ath12k.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/qcom,ath12k.yaml
@@ -13,6 +13,9 @@ maintainers:
 description:
   Qualcomm Technologies IEEE 802.11be PCIe devices.
 
+allOf:
+  - $ref: ieee80211.yaml#
+
 properties:
   compatible:
     enum:
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
index 95988447c22a..30c6ee1a0377 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -14794,9 +14794,11 @@ static int ath12k_mac_hw_register(struct ath12k_hw *ah)
 	u32 ht_cap = U32_MAX, antennas_rx = 0, antennas_tx = 0;
 	bool is_6ghz = false, is_raw_mode = false, is_monitor_disable = false;
 	u8 *mac_addr = NULL;
+	u8 fwnode_mac_addr[ETH_ALEN] = {};
 	u8 mbssid_max_interfaces = 0;
 
 	wiphy->max_ap_assoc_sta = 0;
+	device_get_mac_address(ab->dev, fwnode_mac_addr);
 
 	for_each_ar(ah, ar, i) {
 		u32 ht_cap_info = 0;
@@ -14805,7 +14807,10 @@ static int ath12k_mac_hw_register(struct ath12k_hw *ah)
 		if (ar->ab->pdevs_macaddr_valid) {
 			ether_addr_copy(ar->mac_addr, pdev->mac_addr);
 		} else {
-			ether_addr_copy(ar->mac_addr, ar->ab->mac_addr);
+			if (is_valid_ether_addr(fwnode_mac_addr))
+				ether_addr_copy(ar->mac_addr, fwnode_mac_addr);
+			else
+				ether_addr_copy(ar->mac_addr, ar->ab->mac_addr);
 			ar->mac_addr[4] += ar->pdev_idx;
 		}
 
-- 
